## Real-World Applications

* SQL can be used to track inventory.
* It can connect information from several tables.
* A business can use queries to build reports.
* AI can help write harder SQL queries from a plain-English request.
* The finished query can be added to a program and reused.
* SQL is also useful for jobs involving databases and data analytics.

## Personal Reflection

The main thing I learned from this lecture is that AI can be really useful for SQL.

Some SQL queries can get long and confusing, especially when they need information from several tables. Being able to explain what I want in normal words and have AI create the query can save a lot of time.

I also liked that SQL is easy to test. You can run the query and look at the results right away. If the data is wrong, you know the query needs to be changed. I still think knowing the basics is important because it helps you explain what you want and notice when the AI makes a mistake.

